// KNOWN LIMITATION: "assertion failed" on `f`'s own postcondition, which
// mentions a recursive call `f(n - 1)`.
//
// For `0 < n` the body *is* `f(n - 1)`, so `result ==> f(n - 1)` holds.
// Likely cause (not confirmed): inside its own SCC, Helium routes `f(n - 1)`
// through the uninterpreted limited twin, and the call in the postcondition is
// not identified with the call in the body.
//
// Reduced from `VeC/vercors/publications/RedBlack/Util.java`
// (`method_Util_isPrefix`, `isInfix` and the lemmas over them).
function f(n: Int): Bool
  decreases _
  ensures result && 0 < n ==> f(n - 1)
{
  n <= 0 ? true : f(n - 1)
}
